AWS CloudTrail — The One Service You Can't Afford to Ignore

Every action in your AWS account leaves a footprint. Someone launched an EC2 instance. Someone modified an IAM policy. Someone deleted a production S3 bucket at 2 AM.

The question is — do you have the logs to prove it?🤔

That's exactly what AWS CloudTrail does.🙌

👉It silently records every single API call made in your AWS account — whether it comes from the Console, CLI, SDK, or another AWS service. 

👉It captures WHO did it, WHAT they did, WHEN they did it, WHERE they did it from, and whether it SUCCEEDED or was DENIED.

👉So if you're dealing with compliance — CloudTrail is your audit evidence. Auditors ask "can you prove who did what?" CloudTrail answers that question every time.

👉Bottom line: CloudTrail doesn't just log events. It gives you visibility, accountability, and the forensic power to investigate anything that happens inside your AWS environment.

Start to use it for every incident. ✅

